{"sha":"864d4e593e1d301df5a4ac0d7d7a1c90f0476a67","node_id":"C_kwDOTDJ7sdoAKDg2NGQ0ZTU5M2UxZDMwMWRmNWE0YWMwZDdkN2ExYzkwZjA0NzZhNjc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Scormave","email":"5045197+Scormave@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-10-29T17:58:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"Scormave","email":"5045197+Scormave@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-10-29T17:58:24Z"},"message":"feat: Save many linked records in one transaction with create_records

create_records creates up to 50 repositories, places, sources, notes,
citations, events, people and families in one call. It posts them to
Gramps Web's POST /api/objects/, which saves them in one transaction:
all are created or none, get_recent_changes lists the call as "Add
multiple objects", and one undo_change removes every record.

Each record takes the arguments of its create tool plus an optional
key; other records of the call link to it by "#key" wherever they take
a handle, and a key must name a record of the class the field links
to. People join families only through the family's father, mother and
children, which Gramps Web links back, existing people included. Media
and tags are not created here. Every record is built with the checks
of its create tool before anything is saved, and an error names the
record, e.g. people[1] (key petr). The reply lists each record with its
handle, Gramps ID and key, the existing people that now link back to a
new family, and the events, citations, notes and people left unlinked.
When Gramps Web refuses the call, the error says that none of the
records were saved.

The create tools now build their request bodies in shared
Build*RequestAsync methods that create_records reuses. The argument
filter checks names and types inside the objects of array arguments
too (people[1].birthDate), and turns numbers given for text fields
there into text.

undo_change: Gramps Web's check compares every change with the record
as it is now, so a person added and then linked by a family of the
same transaction was reported as changed later, and the undo was
refused. Such a record now counts once, and its conflicts are dropped
unless every change of the record conflicts.

Gramps Web stores attribute and URL types as objects, and those fields
of GrampsAttribute and GrampsUrl took only strings. A stored person,
event, source, citation or media record with an attribute could not
be read, so undo_change listed such a deleted record by handle alone,
and create_records showed "(no title)" for an existing person that
links back. Both fields now read the string or the object.

The import-from-text prompt and the server instructions point to
create_records. Unit tests cover keys, checks, the request body and
the reply, and the models read records as Gramps Web stores them;
integration tests save a family with its source in one transaction,
undo it, and show that a rejected call writes nothing. Tried on
demo.grampsweb.org (Gramps Web API 3.24.0): save, link back, refusal
and undo, after which the tree matched its earlier state.
README, the site, the tool catalog, the API inventory, the
architecture notes, the system prompt, the MCPB manifest and the
changelog describe the tool; the catalog counts 33 tools.","tree":{"sha":"6eb7e6ff4589e9e3f2692db7c8392bcbf78b7057","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scormave/gramps-web-mcp/git/trees/6eb7e6ff4589e9e3f2692db7c8392bcbf78b7057"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scormave/gramps-web-mcp/git/commits/864d4e593e1d301df5a4ac0d7d7a1c90f0476a67","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scormave/gramps-web-mcp/commits/864d4e593e1d301df5a4ac0d7d7a1c90f0476a67","html_url":"https://github.com/Scormave/gramps-web-mcp/commit/864d4e593e1d301df5a4ac0d7d7a1c90f0476a67","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scormave/gramps-web-mcp/commits/864d4e593e1d301df5a4ac0d7d7a1c90f0476a67/comments","author":{"login":"Scormave","id":5045197,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDUxOTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5045197?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave","html_url":"https://github.com/Scormave","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"Scormave","id":5045197,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDUxOTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5045197?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave","html_url":"https://github.com/Scormave","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scormave/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"86269e6f50718b071b9f15136d8d48876d33caae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scormave/gramps-web-mcp/commits/86269e6f50718b071b9f15136d8d48876d33caae","html_url":"https://github.com/Scormave/gramps-web-mcp/commit/86269e6f50718b071b9f15136d8d48876d33caae"}],"stats":{"total":2555,"additions":2279,"deletions":276},"files":[{"sha":"327e810ad79b7572c3d9659b83f910293169e798","filename":"CHANGELOG.md","status":"modified","additions":32,"deletions":0,"changes":32,"blob_url":"https://github.com/Scormave/gramps-web-mcp/blob/864d4e593e1d301df5a4ac0d7d7a1c90f0476a67/CHANGELOG.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/Scormave/gramps-web-mcp/raw/864d4e593e1d301df5a4ac0d7d7a1c90f0476a67/CHANGELOG.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scormave/gramps-web-mcp/contents/CHANGELOG.md?ref=864d4e593e1d301df5a4ac0d7d7a1c90f0476a67","patch":"@@ -6,8 +6,40 @@ The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/).

 ## [Unreleased]

+### Added
+
+- `create_records`: create up to 50 linked records in one call, such as a
+  family from one register entry with its source, citation and events.
+  Gramps Web saves them in one transaction (`POST /api/objects/`), so
+  either all are created or none, and one `undo_change` on that
+  transaction removes them all. Each record takes the arguments of its
+  create tool plus an optional `key`; other records of the call link to
+  it by `"#key"` wherever they take a handle. People join families
+  through the family's father, mother and children, which get the link
+  back, existing people included. Every record is checked before
+  anything is saved, and an error names the record, e.g. `people[1]`.
+  Argument names and types are checked inside each record as well: an
+  unknown field such as `people[1].birthDate` is named, with a
+  suggestion when one is close
+
+### Changed
+
+- The `import-from-text` prompt saves the new places, source, citation,
+  events, people and families in one `create_records` call instead of
+  one create call per record
+
 ### Fixed

+- `undo_change`: a record the transaction changed more than once, such
+  as a person added and then linked by a family added after it, counts
+  once. Gramps Web's check compares every change with the record as it
+  is now, so such a record was reported as changed after the
+  transaction and the undo was refused
+- `undo_change`: a deleted person, event, source, citation or media
+  record with an attribute, or a deleted person with a web link, is
+  listed by name again instead of by handle alone. Gramps Web stores the
+  attribute and link types as objects, which the record could not be
+  read with
 - `list_objects`: the `gql` description gave the example `gender == 1`,
   which Gramps Web rejects as a syntax error. It now shows `=` for
   equality, lists the operators, says that text goes in double quotes"},{"sha":"8943bea28f2aa125a0a0aea7e073c6e15685aaa0","filename":"GrampsWeb.Mcp.IntegrationTests/RecordBatchTests.cs","status":"added","additions":155,"deletions":0,"changes":155,"blob_url":"https://github.com/Scormave/gramps-web-mcp/blob/864d4e593e1d301df5a4ac0d7d7a1c90f0476a67/GrampsWeb.Mcp.IntegrationTests%2FRecordBatchTests.cs","raw_url":"https://github.com/Scormave/gramps-web-mcp/raw/864d4e593e1d301df5a4ac0d7d7a1c90f0476a67/GrampsWeb.Mcp.IntegrationTests%2FRecordBatchTests.cs","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scormave/gramps-web-mcp/contents/GrampsWeb.Mcp.IntegrationTests%2FRecordBatchTests.cs?ref=864d4e593e1d301df5a4ac0d7d7a1c90f0476a67","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,155 @@
+using System.Text.RegularExpressions;
+using Xunit;
+
+namespace GrampsWeb.Mcp.IntegrationTests;
+
+[Collection(GrampsWebCollection.Name)]
+public sealed class RecordBatchTests(GrampsWebFixture gramps)
+{
+    private McpSession Session => gramps.Session;
+
+    [IntegrationFact]
+    public async Task CreateRecords_SavesAFamilyWithItsSourcesInOneTransaction()
+    {
+        var surname = TestNames.Surname();
+        var title = TestNames.Surname() + " metric book";
+        var mother = await Session.CreateAsync("create_person", new
+        {
+            primaryName = new { first = "Maria", surname = TestNames.Surname() },
+            gender = "female"
+        });
+
+        var result = await Session.CallAsync("create_records", new
+        {
+            sources = new[] { new { key = "book", title } },
+            citations = new[] { new { key = "entry", sourceHandle = "#book", page = "f. 12, No. 34", date = "1890" } },
+            events = new[]
+            {
+                new { key = "birth", eventType = "Birth", date = "1890-05-03", citationHandles = new[] { "#entry" } },
+                new { key = "marriage", eventType = "Marriage", date = "about 1884", citationHandles = Array.Empty<string>() }
+            },
+            people = new object[]
+            {
+                new { key = "ivan", primaryName = new { first = "Ivan", surname }, gender = "male" },
+                new { key = "petr", primaryName = new { first = "Petr", surname }, gender = "male", eventRefs = new[] { "#birth" } }
+            },
+            families = new[]
+            {
+                new
+                {
+                    key = "family",
+                    fatherHandle = "#ivan",
+                    motherHandle = mother.GrampsId,
+                    eventRefs = new[] { "#marriage::Family" },
+                    childRefs = new[] { "#petr" }
+                }
+            }
+        });
+
+        Assert.Equal("created", McpSession.Header(result, "action"));
+        Assert.Equal("7", McpSession.Header(result, "records"));
+        Assert.Contains("Existing records that now link back to a new family (1):", result);
+        Assert.Contains($"— handle: {mother.Handle} | gramps_id: {mother.GrampsId}", result);
+        Assert.DoesNotContain("Not linked from any record of this call", result);
+        var changes = await Session.CallAsync("get_recent_changes", new { limit = 1 });
+        Assert.Contains("Add multiple objects", changes);
+
+        var father = Record(result, "ivan");
+        var son = Record(result, "petr");
+        var family = Record(result, "family");
+        var storedFamily = await Session.CallAsync("get_object", new { identifier = family.GrampsId });
+        Assert.Contains($"Father: {surname}, Ivan ({father.GrampsId})", storedFamily);
+        Assert.Contains($"({mother.GrampsId})", storedFamily);
+        Assert.Contains("Marriage: about 1884", storedFamily);
+        Assert.Contains("Children (1):", storedFamily);
+        Assert.Contains($"({son.GrampsId}) [handle: {son.Handle}], b. 1890-05-03", storedFamily);
+
+        Assert.Contains($"[handle: {family.Handle}]", await Session.CallAsync("get_object", new { identifier = son.GrampsId }));
+        Assert.Contains($"[handle: {family.Handle}]", await Session.CallAsync("get_object", new { identifier = mother.GrampsId }));
+
+        var storedBirth = await Session.CallAsync("get_object", new { identifier = Record(result, "birth").GrampsId });
+        Assert.Contains(Record(result, "entry").Handle, storedBirth);
+        var storedCitation = await Session.CallAsync("get_object", new { identifier = Record(result, "entry").GrampsId });
+        Assert.Contains($"Source: {title} [handle: {Record(result, "book").Handle}]", storedCitation);
+    }
+
+    [IntegrationFact]
+    public async Task Undo_OfCreateRecords_RemovesEveryRecord()
+    {
+        var surname = TestNames.Surname();
+        var result = await Session.CallAsync("create_records", new
+        {
+            events = new[] { new { key = "birth", eventType = "Birth", date = "1885" } },
+            people = new object[]
+            {
+                new { key = "ivan", primaryName = new { first = "Ivan", surname }, gender = "male" },
+                new { key = "anna", primaryName = new { first = "Anna", surname }, gender = "female", eventRefs = new[] { "#birth" } }
+            },
+            families = new[] { new { key = "family", fatherHandle = "#ivan", childRefs = new[] { "#anna" } } }
+        });
+        var transaction = await LatestTransactionAsync();
+
+        // The family links both people back in the same transaction, which must not count as a later change.
+        var check = await Session.CallAsync("undo_change", new { transactionId = transaction, dryRun = true });
+        Assert.Equal("0", McpSession.Header(check, "conflicts"));
+
+        var undone = await Session.CallAsync("undo_change", new { transactionId = transaction });
+
+        Assert.Equal("undone", McpSession.Header(undone, "action"));
+        foreach (var key in new[] { "birth", "ivan", "anna", "family" })
+        {
+            var record = Record(result, key);
+            Assert.Contains($"not found: {record.GrampsId}", await Session.CallAsync("get_object", new { identifier = record.GrampsId }));
+        }
+    }
+
+    [IntegrationFact]
+    public async Task CreateRecords_ThatGrampsWebRejects_WritesNothing()
+    {
+        var surname = TestNames.Surname();
+        var before = await LatestTransactionAsync();
+
+        // The family is saved after both people, and Gramps Web fails it on the child that does not exist.
+        var error = await Session.CallErrorAsync("create_records", new
+        {
+            people = new[] { new { key = "ivan", primaryName = new { first = "Ivan", surname }, gender = "male" } },
+            families = new[] { new { fatherHandle = "#ivan", childRefs = new[] { "nosuchperson0000" } } }
+        });
+
+        Assert.Contains("Gramps Web refused the call and saved none of the records.", error);
+        Assert.Equal(before, await LatestTransactionAsync());
+        Assert.Contains("No results found", await Session.CallAsync("search", new { query = surname }));
+    }
+
+    [IntegrationFact]
+    public async Task CreateRecords_WithABadKey_WritesNothing()
+    {
+        var before = await LatestTransactionAsync();
+
+        var error = await Session.CallErrorAsync("create_records", new
+        {
+            notes = new[] { new { key = "note", text = TestNames.Unique("note") } },
+            people = new[] { new { primaryName = new { first = "Ivan", surname = TestNames.Surname() }, noteHandles = new[] { "#nota" } } }
+        });
+
+        Assert.Contains("has \"#nota\", which is not a key of this call. Keys of note records in this call: #note.", error);
+        Assert.Equal(before, await LatestTransactionAsync());
+    }
+
+    /// <summary>The handle and Gramps ID of the record the call gave <paramref name="key"/>.</summary>
+    private static (string Handle, string GrampsId) Record(string result, string key)
+    {
+        var match = Regex.Match(result, $@"— handle: (\S+) \| gramps_id: (\S+) \| key: {Regex.Escape(key)}\r?$",
+            RegexOptions.Multiline);
+        Assert.True(match.Success, $"No record with key {key} in:\n{result}");
+        return (match.Groups[1].Value, match.Groups[2].Value);
+    }
+
+    private async Task<int> LatestTransactionAsync()
+    {
+        var changes = await Session.CallAsync("get_recent_changes", new { limit = 1 });
+        var match = Regex.Match(changes, @"\[transaction: (\d+)\]");
+        Assert.True(match.Success, $"No transaction number in:\n{changes}");
+        return int.Parse(match.Groups[1].Value);
+    }
+}"},{"sha":"680fdb6cc1de9bef57702fd0ccc56b089cc3fe6f","filename":"GrampsWeb.Mcp.Tests/UnitTests/GrampsCompatibilityDeserializeTests.cs","status":"modified","additions":115,"deletions":0,"changes":115,"blob_url":"https://github.com/Scormave/gramps-web-mcp/blob/864d4e593e1d301df5a4ac0d7d7a1c90f0476a67/GrampsWeb.Mcp.Tests%2FUnitTests%2FGrampsCompatibilityDeserializeTests.cs","raw_url":"https://github.com/Scormave/gramps-web-mcp/raw/864d4e593e1d301df5a4ac0d7d7a1c90f0476a67/GrampsWeb.Mcp.Tests%2FUnitTests%2FGrampsCompatibilityDeserializeTests.cs","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scormave/gramps-web-mcp/contents/GrampsWeb.Mcp.Tests%2FUnitTests%2FGrampsCompatibilityDeserializeTests.cs?ref=864d4e593e1d301df5a4ac0d7d7a1c90f0476a67","patch":"@@ -375,4 +375,119 @@ public void Serialize_DateRequest_RoundTripsDateval()
         Assert.Equal(2003, arr[2].GetInt32());
         Assert.False(arr[3].GetBoolean());
     }
+
+    private const string RawDate =
+        """{ "_class": "Date", "format": null, "calendar": 0, "modifier": 0, "quality": 0, "dateval": [0, 0, 1862, false], "text": "", "sortval": 2401142, "newyear": 0 }""";
+
+    private const string RawAttribute =
+        """{ "_class": "Attribute", "private": false, "type": { "_class": "AttributeType", "value": 0, "string": "RIN" }, "value": "MH:I178", "citation_list": [], "note_list": [] }""";
+
+    private const string RawSourceAttribute =
+        """{ "_class": "SrcAttribute", "private": false, "type": { "_class": "SrcAttributeType", "value": -1, "string": "Fond" }, "value": "Ф.230" }""";
+
+    private const string RawUrl =
+        """{ "_class": "Url", "private": false, "path": "https://example.org", "desc": "Home page", "type": { "_class": "UrlType", "value": 2, "string": "" } }""";
+
+    /// <summary>
+    /// Records as Gramps 6 stores them (transaction history old data, the new data POST /api/objects/ returns):
+    /// every typed field is an object, where a GET gives a string.
